arXiv:2603.29380v1 [cs.LG] 31 Mar 2026</div>
</div><div class="ltx_page_content">
<article class="ltx_document ltx_authors_1line">
<h1 class="ltx_title ltx_font_bold ltx_title_document" style="font-size:120%;">Finite-time analysis of Multi-timescale Stochastic Optimization Algorithms</h1>
<div class="ltx_authors">
<span class="ltx_creator ltx_role_author">
<span class="ltx_personname">Kaustubh Kartikey
</span></span>
<span class="ltx_author_before">  </span><span class="ltx_creator ltx_role_author">
<span class="ltx_personname">Shalabh Bhatnagar
</span></span></div>

<div id="abstract1" class="ltx_abstract"><h6 class="ltx_title ltx_title_abstract">Abstract</h6>
    
<p id="abstract1.1" class="ltx_p">We present a finite-time analysis of two smoothed functional stochastic approximation algorithms for simulation-based optimization. The first is a two time-scale gradient-based method, while the second is a three time-scale Newton-based algorithm that estimates both the gradient and the Hessian of the objective function <math id="abstract1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>J</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J</annotation></semantics></math>. Both algorithms involve zeroth order estimates for the gradient/Hessian. Although the asymptotic convergence of these algorithms has been established in prior work, finite-time guarantees of two-timescale stochastic optimization algorithms in zeroth order settings have not been provided previously. For our Newton algorithm, we derive mean-squared error bounds for the Hessian estimator and establish a finite-time bound on <math id="abstract1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min\limits_{0\leq m\leq T}\mathbb{E}\|\nabla J(\theta(m))\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>𝔼</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min\limits_{0\leq m\leq T}\mathbb{E}\|\nabla J(\theta(m))\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, showing convergence to first-order stationary points. The analysis explicitly characterizes the interaction between multiple time-scales and the propagation of estimation errors. We further identify step-size choices that balance dominant error terms and achieve near-optimal convergence rates. We also provide corresponding finite-time guarantees for the gradient algorithm under the same framework. The theoretical results are further validated through experiments on the Continuous Mountain Car environment.</p>
  
</div>
<section id="S1" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">1 </span>INTRODUCTION</h2>

<div id="S1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Stochastic approximation (SA) methods form the backbone of simulation-based optimization, reinforcement learning, and adaptive control algorithms, where objective functions and gradients are not available in closed form but can be estimated through noisy observations. While gradient-based algorithms such as stochastic gradient descent and simultaneous perturbation stochastic approximation (SPSA) are widely used due to their simplicity and robustness, their convergence can be slow in ill-conditioned problems. This has motivated the development of Newton-based stochastic methods that aim to exploit curvature information to improve convergence speed and stability. In cases where the gradient and/or Hessian of the sample performance objective is not known in closed form, zeroth-order stochastic optimization approaches <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">14</a>]</cite> help by providing suitable forms of the gradient/Hessian estimates based on noisy performance samples.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Newton-type stochastic approximation algorithms that estimate the Hessian or its inverse using noisy function evaluations have attracted significant attention recently. Notable examples include Newton-based simultaneous perturbation stochastic approximation (SPSA) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">12</a>, <a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">13</a>]</cite> and smoothed functional (SF)–based methods such as the Newton smoothed functional (NSF) algorithms <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">6</a>]</cite>. These methods typically operate on multiple time-scales, with the Hessian estimator evolving on a faster time-scale than the parameter updates as it helps obtain the Hessian inverse post the averaging on the Hessian. Although the asymptotic convergence properties of these previously proposed algorithms are well understood, their analysis of finite-time behavior remains limited or unknown.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Finite-time convergence analysis has been extensively studied for single timescale gradient-based stochastic optimization methods, including nonconvex settings, where bounds on the expected gradient norm or function suboptimality are available <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">14</a>]</cite>. However, extending such analyses to multi-timescale, Newton-based algorithms is challenging due to the coupling between parameter updates and the noisy Hessian estimates.
In particular, note that the Hessian is learned on a faster time-scale while the parameter updates depend on its inverse and proceed on a slower scale. Thus, bounding the transient error of the Hessian estimator and quantifying its impact on the optimization dynamics requires analysis of multiple interacting stochastic recursions.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">This paper addresses this problem by providing a finite-time analysis of a three-timescale Newton smoothed functional (NSF1) algorithm. We focus on bounding both the mean-squared error of the Hessian estimator and the expected norm of the gradient over a <math id="S1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>-length horizon, thereby establishing convergence to first-order stationary points with explicit rates.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">The main contributions of this paper are summarized as follows:</p>
<ul id="S1.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We derive finite-time mean-squared error bounds for the Hessian estimator in the NSF1 algorithm, explicitly accounting for both diagonal and off-diagonal estimation errors.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Using these bounds, we establish a finite-time convergence guarantee on
<math id="S1.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min\limits_{0\leq m\leq T}\mathbb{E}\|\nabla J(\theta(m))\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>𝔼</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min\limits_{0\leq m\leq T}\mathbb{E}\|\nabla J(\theta(m))\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, demonstrating convergence to
first-order stationary points.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S1.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S1.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We characterize the interaction between multiple timescale recursions and identify
near-optimal step-size exponents that balance the dominant error terms so as to minimize the sample complexity
and yield near-optimal finite-time rates.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S1.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S1.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Numerical experiments validate the theoretical decay rates and illustrate the benefits
of curvature-aware updates compared to purely gradient-based stochastic methods.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">2 </span>Related Work</h2>

<div id="S2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This work analyzes stochastic approximation algorithms involving smoothed functional gradient/Hessian estimators, for their finite-time behavior.
We briefly review the most relevant literature and state our contributions relative to existing results.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Classical stochastic approximation was introduced in the seminal work of  <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">1</a>]</cite> and has since been extensively studied. Finite-time convergence guarantees for first-order stochastic optimization methods, including nonconvex settings, are now well understood. Results include convergence rate analyses for stochastic gradient descent and mirror descent  <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">2</a>, <a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">3</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">These analyses typically assume access to unbiased (or biased but controlled) gradient estimates and primarily conducted for algorithms that operate on a single time-scale. In contrast, the algorithms studied in this paper rely solely on noisy function evaluations and involve multi-timescale stochastic iterates. As a result, existing finite-time bounds for first-order methods are not directly applicable to the setting considered here.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Smoothed functional (SF) and simultaneous perturbation stochastic approximation (SPSA) methods provide gradient and Hessian estimates using random perturbations and noisy function evaluations. Early developments include SPSA <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">4</a>]</cite> and SF-based methods for simulation optimization <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">5</a>]</cite>. Second-order extensions, including Newton SPSA and Newton smoothed functional (NSF) algorithms, were developed in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">12</a>, <a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">13</a>, <a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">6</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Most existing analyses of SF and SPSA methods focus on providing asymptotic convergence guarantees, establishing almost sure convergence or convergence in probability under standard stochastic approximation assumptions.
While these results provide important theoretical guarantees, they do not yield explicit finite-time error bounds for the gradient or Hessian estimates. In particular, finite-time mean-squared error bounds for Hessian estimators in NSF-type algorithms have remained largely unexplored.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Second-order stochastic approximation methods are known to improve conditioning and convergence behavior compared to first-order methods, especially in ill-conditioned problems. Classical treatments of second-order stochastic approximation rely on ODE-based or weak convergence arguments <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">7</a>, <a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">8</a>, <a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">9</a>]</cite>. These analyses are inherently asymptotic and do not quantify transient behavior.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p7.1" class="ltx_p">Our work complements this literature by providing the first explicit finite-time bounds for Newton-type smoothed functional algorithms. Unlike prior asymptotic results, we explicitly characterize the evolution of the Hessian estimation error and quantify its impact on the optimization dynamics over a horizon of length <math id="S2.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p8.1" class="ltx_p">Multi-timescale stochastic approximation has been widely studied in the context of adaptive control and reinforcement learning (RL) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">11</a>, <a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">10</a>, <a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">9</a>]</cite>. These works establish asymptotic convergence using ODE and differential inclusion
techniques and have been successfully applied to actor-critic and policy-gradient algorithms.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p9.1" class="ltx_p">Finite-time analysis of multi-timescale algorithms even in the context of RL, however, is significantly more challenging and remains relatively limited.
Existing results largely focus on first-order methods (see <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">14</a>]</cite>) or special linear settings. To the best of our knowledge, finite-time convergence guarantees for multi-timescale, second-order smoothed functional algorithms have not been previously established.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p10.1" class="ltx_p">The results in this paper can be viewed as a finite-time counterpart to existing asymptotic analyses of NSF algorithms. Compared to first-order smoothed functional methods such as GSF1, our analysis demonstrates how incorporating curvature information improves convergence behavior
under comparable oracle and noise assumptions. While the resulting rates are generally slower than those obtained for stochastic gradient methods with exact (noisy) gradient access, they are achieved under substantially
weaker information models, relying only on noisy function evaluations and random perturbations.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p11.1" class="ltx_p">In summary, this work fills a major gap that previously existed by providing the first finite-time analysis of Newton-based multi-timescale stochastic optimization algorithms.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">3 </span>NSF1 and GSF1 Algorithms</h2>

<div id="S3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we describe the Newton Smoothed Functional (NSF1) algorithm, a three–time–scale stochastic approximation method that simultaneously estimates the Hessian and gradient of the objective function using noisy function measurements and performs curvature-aware parameter updates. The algorithm is designed to ensure that curvature information is tracked rapidly, while the parameters evolve on a slower time-scale to guarantee stability.</p>
</div>
<section id="S3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.1 </span>Problem Setup</h3>

<div id="S3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We consider the unconstrained stochastic optimization problem</p>
<table id="S3.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min_{\theta\in\mathbb{R}^{d}}J(\theta)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min_{\theta\in\mathbb{R}^{d}}J(\theta),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\displaystyle J(\theta)=\lim_{N\rightarrow\infty}\frac{1}{N}\mathbb{E}[\sum_{m=0}^{N-1}h(\theta,X_{m})]=\sum_{s\in S}d_{\theta}(s)h(\theta,s)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">lim</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle J(\theta)=\lim_{N\rightarrow\infty}\frac{1}{N}\mathbb{E}[\sum_{m=0}^{N-1}h(\theta,X_{m})]=\sum_{s\in S}d_{\theta}(s)h(\theta,s)}</annotation></semantics></math> is a long-run average over single-stage costs <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h(\theta,X_{m})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h(\theta,X_{m})</annotation></semantics></math> that depend on a parameter <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math> and where given any parameter <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{X_{m}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{X_{m}\}</annotation></semantics></math> is an ergodic Markov chain with transition probabilities <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\theta}(s,s^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\theta}(s,s^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s,s^{\prime}\in S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s,s^{\prime}\in S</annotation></semantics></math> with stationary distribution <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\theta}(s),s\in S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\theta}(s),s\in S</annotation></semantics></math>. For simplicity, we assume <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> to be a finite set.
The objective function <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math> and its derivatives are not directly observable;
instead, noisy samples <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h(\theta,X_{m})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h(\theta,X_{m})</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, are available.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.2 </span>Smoothed Functional Gradient and Hessian Estimation</h3>

<div id="S3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\eta(m)\}_{m\geq 0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\eta(m)\}_{m\geq 0}</annotation></semantics></math> be an i.i.d. sequence of <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>-dimensional random vectors with each component being distributed <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>.
For a smoothing parameter <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, the smoothed functional gradient estimator is defined as</p>
<table id="S3.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z(m)=\frac{\eta(m)}{\beta}\,h(\theta(m)+\beta\eta(m),X_{m})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>β</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z(m)=\frac{\eta(m)}{\beta}\,h(\theta(m)+\beta\eta(m),X_{m}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The smoothed functional Hessian estimator is defined element-wise as</p>
<table id="S3.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{H}_{i,i}(m)=\frac{\eta_{i}^{2}(m)-1}{\beta^{2}}\,h(\theta(m)+\beta\eta(m),X_{m})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{H}_{i,i}(m)=\frac{\eta_{i}^{2}(m)-1}{\beta^{2}}\,h(\theta(m)+\beta\eta(m),X_{m}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><math id="S3.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1,\ldots,d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1,\ldots,d</annotation></semantics></math> and</p>
<table id="S3.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{H}_{i,j}(m)=\frac{\eta_{i}(m)\eta_{j}(m)}{\beta^{2}}\,h(\theta(m)+\beta\eta(m),X_{m}),\quad i\neq j." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{H}_{i,j}(m)=\frac{\eta_{i}(m)\eta_{j}(m)}{\beta^{2}}\,h(\theta(m)+\beta\eta(m),X_{m}),\quad i\neq j.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p2.3" class="ltx_p">As shown in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">6</a>]</cite>, these estimators provide unbiased estimates of the gradient and Hessian of the
Gaussian-smoothed objective in the limit as <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\rightarrow 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\rightarrow 0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.3 </span>Recursive Hessian Tracking (Fastest Time-Scale)</h3>

<div id="S3.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The Hessian estimate is updated recursively as</p>
<table id="S3.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(m+1)=H(m)+b(m)\big(\hat{H}(m)-H(m)\big)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(m+1)=H(m)+b(m)\big(\hat{H}(m)-H(m)\big),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{H}(m)=[[\hat{H}_{i,j}(m)]]_{i,j=1}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{H}(m)=[[\hat{H}_{i,j}(m)]]_{i,j=1}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="S3.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;b(m)\rightarrow 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;b(m)\rightarrow 0</annotation></semantics></math> slowest amongst all the step-size schedules, making the recursion governed by <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b(m)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b(m)</annotation></semantics></math> the fastest timescale recursion.
This update ensures that the Hessian estimator rapidly tracks
<math id="S3.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla^{2}J(\theta(m))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mo>∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla^{2}J(\theta(m))</annotation></semantics></math> (see <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">6</a>]</cite> for details).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.4 </span>Gradient Tracking (Intermediate Time-Scale)</h3>

<div id="S3.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In addition to Hessian tracking, the NSF1 algorithm maintains a recursive estimate
of the gradient on an intermediate time-scale.
Let <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z(m)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z(m)</annotation></semantics></math> denote the gradient estimate.
Using smoothed functional perturbations, an instantaneous gradient observation is given by</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S3.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{g}(m)=\frac{\eta(m)}{\beta}\,h(\theta(m)+\beta\eta(m),X_{m})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>β</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{g}(m)=\frac{\eta(m)}{\beta}\,h(\theta(m)+\beta\eta(m),X_{m}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The gradient estimate is updated recursively as</p>
<table id="S3.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z(m+1)=Z(m)+c(m)\big(\hat{g}(m)-Z(m)\big)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z(m+1)=Z(m)+c(m)\big(\hat{g}(m)-Z(m)\big),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS4.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c(m)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c(m)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> is a diminishing step-size satisfying</p>
<table id="S3.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a(m)=o(c(m))\text{ and }c(m)=o(b(m))." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> and </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a(m)=o(c(m))\text{ and }c(m)=o(b(m)).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS4.p2.3" class="ltx_p">This recursion allows the gradient estimator to track
<math id="S3.SS4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla J(\theta(m))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla J(\theta(m))</annotation></semantics></math> on a time-scale slower than the Hessian estimation
but faster than the parameter updates.
Under standard smoothness assumptions, in the limit as <math id="S3.SS4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\rightarrow 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\rightarrow 0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.SS4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z(m)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z(m)</annotation></semantics></math> converges to the true gradient
<math id="S3.SS4.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla J(\theta(m))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla J(\theta(m))</annotation></semantics></math> sufficiently fast so that its tracking error does not
dominate the parameter dynamics.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.5 </span>Parameter Update (Slowest Time-Scale)</h3>

<div id="S3.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The parameter update is given by</p>
<table id="S3.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta(m+1)=\Gamma(\theta(m)-a(m)\,M(m)\,Z(m))," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta(m+1)=\Gamma(\theta(m)-a(m)\,M(m)\,Z(m)),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS5.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M(m)=(P_{\text{PD}}(H(m)))^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>PD</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M(m)=(P_{\text{PD}}(H(m)))^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math> with
<math id="S3.SS5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\text{PD}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>PD</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\text{PD}}</annotation></semantics></math> being an operator that projects any matrix to the space of positive definite matrices. This may correspond to the Choleski factorization procedure. It could correspond to
<math id="S3.SS5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M(m)=(H(m)+\lambda I)^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M(m)=(H(m)+\lambda I)^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math> for a small enough <math id="S3.SS5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.
This projection is needed to ensure the updates in the descent direction guided by the Newton step.
Also, in the above, <math id="S3.SS5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma:\mathbb{R}^{d}\rightarrow C\subset\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma:\mathbb{R}^{d}\rightarrow C\subset\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> is a projection operator to a prespecified compact and convex set <math id="S3.SS5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span> Newton Smoothed Functional (NSF1) Algorithm</figcaption>
<div id="alg1.3" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg1.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">1:</span></span>
              
            Initial parameter <math id="alg1.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta(0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta(0)</annotation></semantics></math>, initial Hessian estimate <math id="alg1.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(0)</annotation></semantics></math>, smoothing parameter <math id="alg1.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, total iterations <math id="alg1.l1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">2:</span></span>
              
            Step-sizes: <math id="alg1.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a(t)=(1+t)^{-\sigma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a(t)=(1+t)^{-\sigma}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg1.l2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b(t)=(1+t)^{-\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b(t)=(1+t)^{-\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg1.l2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c(t)=(1+t)^{-\nu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c(t)=(1+t)^{-\nu}</annotation></semantics></math>, with <math id="alg1.l2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\nu&lt;\alpha&lt;\sigma&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>ν</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\nu&lt;\alpha&lt;\sigma&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">3:</span></span>
              
            <span id="alg1.l3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg1.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=0</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="alg1.l3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T-1</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">4:</span></span>
              
              Sample perturbations <math id="alg1.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{i}(t)\sim\mathcal{N}(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{i}(t)\sim\mathcal{N}(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg1.l4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1,\ldots,d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1,\ldots,d</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="alg1.l4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta(t)=(\eta_{i}(t),i=1,2,\ldots,d)^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta(t)=(\eta_{i}(t),i=1,2,\ldots,d)^{T}</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">5:</span></span>
              
              Generate <math id="alg1.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X(t)</annotation></semantics></math> using the perturbed parameter <math id="alg1.l5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\theta(t)+\eta(t))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\theta(t)+\eta(t))</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">6:</span></span>
              
              <span id="alg1.l6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Estimate the smoothed Hessian (using a moving average):</span>
for <math id="alg1.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i,j,k=1,2,\ldots,d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i,j,k=1,2,\ldots,d</annotation></semantics></math>,

<table id="S3.Ex5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex5X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex5X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle H_{i,i}(t+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle H_{i,i}(t+1)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex5X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=H_{i,i}(t)+b(t)\Big(\frac{\eta_{i}^{2}(t)-1}{\beta^{2}}h(X(t))-" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0em">−</mo></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=H_{i,i}(t)+b(t)\Big(\frac{\eta_{i}^{2}(t)-1}{\beta^{2}}h(X(t))-</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex5Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex5Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle H_{i,i}(t)\Big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle H_{i,i}(t)\Big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright" colspan="2"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>For <math id="alg1.l6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k&lt;j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k&lt;j</annotation></semantics></math>,

<table id="S3.Ex6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex6X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex6X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle H_{j,k}(t+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle H_{j,k}(t+1)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex6X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=H_{j,k}(t)+b(t)\Big(\frac{\eta_{j}(t)\eta_{k}(t)-1}{\beta^{2}}h(X(t))-" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0em">−</mo></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=H_{j,k}(t)+b(t)\Big(\frac{\eta_{j}(t)\eta_{k}(t)-1}{\beta^{2}}h(X(t))-</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex6Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex6Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle H_{j,k}(t)\Big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle H_{j,k}(t)\Big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright" colspan="2"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>For <math id="alg1.l6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j&lt;k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j&lt;k</annotation></semantics></math>, set
<math id="alg1.l6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{j,k}(t+1)=H_{k,j}(t+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{j,k}(t+1)=H_{k,j}(t+1)</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l7.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">7:</span></span>
              
              Project Hessian to ensure positive definiteness:

<table id="S3.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(t+1)\leftarrow P_{\text{PD}}\big(H(t+1)\big)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>PD</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(t+1)\leftarrow P_{\text{PD}}\big(H(t+1)\big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l8.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">8:</span></span>
              
              <span id="alg1.l8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Estimate the smoothed gradient:</span>

<table id="S3.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z(t+1)=Z(t)+c(t)\left(\frac{\eta(t)}{\beta}h(X(t))-Z(t)\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>β</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z(t+1)=Z(t)+c(t)\left(\frac{\eta(t)}{\beta}h(X(t))-Z(t)\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l9.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">9:</span></span>
              
              Update parameter using a damped Newton step:
<math id="alg1.l9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta(t+1)=\Gamma(\theta(t)-a(t)\,H^{-1}(t+1)\,Z(t+1))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta(t+1)=\Gamma(\theta(t)-a(t)\,H^{-1}(t+1)\,Z(t+1))</annotation></semantics></math>
where <math id="alg1.l9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math> is the projection operator.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l10.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">10:</span></span>
              
            <span id="alg1.l10.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l10.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l11.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">11:</span></span>
              
            <span id="alg1.l11.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span> Final parameter <math id="alg1.l11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta(T)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta(T)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
</div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS6" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.6 </span>The GSF1 Algorithm</h3>

<div id="S3.SS6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In addition to NSF1, we also analyze the Gradient Smoothed Functional (GSF1)
algorithm, which is a zeroth-order two-timescale stochastic gradient scheme.
GSF1 employs smoothed functional perturbations to estimate the gradient of the
objective function and updates the parameters using this estimate alone. The gradient estimation <math id="S3.SS6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla J(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla J(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math> is done using (<a href="#S3.E4" title="In 3.4 Gradient Tracking (Intermediate Time-Scale) ‣ 3 NSF1 and GSF1 Algorithms ‣ Finite-time analysis of Multi-timescale Stochastic Optimization Algorithms" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>)-(<a href="#S3.E5" title="In 3.4 Gradient Tracking (Intermediate Time-Scale) ‣ 3 NSF1 and GSF1 Algorithms ‣ Finite-time analysis of Multi-timescale Stochastic Optimization Algorithms" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>). The parameter update however is now the following:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta(m+1)=\Gamma(\theta(m)-a(m)\,Z(m))." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta(m+1)=\Gamma(\theta(m)-a(m)\,Z(m)).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS6.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS6.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The finite-time bounds that we develop apply directly
to GSF1 by specializing the analysis to the case without Hessian estimation.
This allows us to provide finite-time convergence guarantees for both first-
and second-order smoothed functional methods under a unified set of assumptions.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S4" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">4 </span>Assumptions</h2>

<div id="S4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we state the assumptions used throughout the finite-time analysis.
All assumptions are standard in stochastic approximation and smoothed functional
optimization and are sufficient to establish the results for both NSF1 and GSF1.
Recall that the long-run average cost is</p>
<table id="S4.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J(\theta)=\lim_{n\to\infty}\frac{1}{n}\mathbb{E}_{\theta}\left[\sum_{t=0}^{n-1}h(\theta,X_{t})\right]=\pi_{\theta}^{T}h_{\theta}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">lim</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J(\theta)=\lim_{n\to\infty}\frac{1}{n}\mathbb{E}_{\theta}\left[\sum_{t=0}^{n-1}h(\theta,X_{t})\right]=\pi_{\theta}^{T}h_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> is the stationary distribution and <math id="S4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{\theta}=[h(\theta,1),\dots,h(\theta,N)]^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{\theta}=[h(\theta,1),\dots,h(\theta,N)]^{T}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmassumption1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_assumption">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmassumption1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Assumption 1</span></span><span id="Thmassumption1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmassumption1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmassumption1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmassumption1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For all <math id="Thmassumption1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta\in C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta\in C</annotation></semantics></math>, the chain is irreducible and aperiodic. The fundamental matrix <math id="Thmassumption1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{\theta}=(I-P_{\theta}+\mathbf{1}\pi_{\theta}^{T})^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>𝟏</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{\theta}=(I-P_{\theta}+\mathbf{1}\pi_{\theta}^{T})^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math> is well-defined and satisfies <math id="Thmassumption1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sup_{\theta\in C}\|Z_{\theta}\|&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>sup</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sup_{\theta\in C}\|Z_{\theta}\|&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmassumption2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_assumption">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmassumption2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Assumption 2</span></span><span id="Thmassumption2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmassumption2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmassumption2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmassumption2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The mappings <math id="Thmassumption2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta\mapsto P(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta\mapsto P(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmassumption2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta\mapsto h_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta\mapsto h_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> are <math id="Thmassumption2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{3}</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="Thmassumption2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence, <math id="Thmassumption2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Thmassumption2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>, and their first, second and third derivatives are uniformly bounded on <math id="Thmassumption2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The following lemma provides smoothness and regularity conditions on the function <math id="S4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>J</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J</annotation></semantics></math> and builds on the results in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">15</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 1</span></span><span id="Thmlemma1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under Assumptions <a href="#Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 1. ‣ 4 Assumptions ‣ Finite-time analysis of Multi-timescale Stochastic Optimization Algorithms" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> and <a href="#Thmassumption2" title="Assumption 2. ‣ 4 Assumptions ‣ Finite-time analysis of Multi-timescale Stochastic Optimization Algorithms" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla J(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla J(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla^{2}J(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mo>∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla^{2}J(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math> are both Lipschitz continuous on <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">We show it for the case of <math id="S4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla J(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla J(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math> as similar arguments extend to the case of <math id="S4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla^{2}J(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mo>∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla^{2}J(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Differentiating the identity <math id="S4.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta}^{T}(I-P_{\theta})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}^{T}(I-P_{\theta})=0</annotation></semantics></math> with respect to <math id="S4.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> yields:</span></p>
<table id="S4.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\theta}\pi_{\theta}^{T}(I-P_{\theta})=\pi_{\theta}^{T}\nabla_{\theta}P_{\theta}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\theta}\pi_{\theta}^{T}(I-P_{\theta})=\pi_{\theta}^{T}\nabla_{\theta}P_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">Post-multiplying by <math id="S4.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> and noting that <math id="S4.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\theta}\pi_{\theta}^{T}\mathbf{1}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>𝟏</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\theta}\pi_{\theta}^{T}\mathbf{1}=0</annotation></semantics></math> (where <math id="S4.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>𝟏</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{1}</annotation></semantics></math> is the vector of all 1’s) gives</span></p>
<table id="S4.E8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\theta}\pi_{\theta}^{T}=\pi_{\theta}^{T}(\nabla_{\theta}P_{\theta})Z_{\theta}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\theta}\pi_{\theta}^{T}=\pi_{\theta}^{T}(\nabla_{\theta}P_{\theta})Z_{\theta}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">Then,</span></p>
<table id="S4.E9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E9.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\nabla J(\theta)=\nabla\pi_{\theta}^{T}h_{\theta}+\pi_{\theta}^{T}\nabla h_{\theta}=\pi_{\theta}^{T}(\nabla P_{\theta})Z_{\theta}h_{\theta}+\pi_{\theta}^{T}\nabla h_{\theta}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>J</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla J(\theta)=\nabla\pi_{\theta}^{T}h_{\theta}+\pi_{\theta}^{T}\nabla h_{\theta}=\pi_{\theta}^{T}(\nabla P_{\theta})Z_{\theta}h_{\theta}+\pi_{\theta}^{T}\nabla h_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">By the mean-value theorem, <math id="S4.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla J(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla J(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math> is Lipschitz continuous if <math id="S4.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla^{2}J(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mo>∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla^{2}J(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math>) is uniformly bounded on <math id="S4.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>. The components of <math id="S4.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla^{2}J(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mo>∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla^{2}J(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math> involve terms of the form:
<math id="S4.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla P_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla P_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla^{2}P_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mo>∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla^{2}P_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla h_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla h_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla^{2}h_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mo>∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla^{2}h_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>.
By Assumptions <a href="#Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 1. ‣ 4 Assumptions ‣ Finite-time analysis of Multi-timescale Stochastic Optimization Algorithms" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>-<a href="#Thmassumption2" title="Assumption 2. ‣ 4 Assumptions ‣ Finite-time analysis of Multi-timescale Stochastic Optimization Algorithms" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, each of the above terms is continuous and bounded on <math id="S4.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="S4.p4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> is an inverse of a matrix whose determinant is non-zero (due to ergodicity), it is also <math id="S4.p4.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S4.p4.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math>. Also,
as <math id="S4.p4.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla^{2}J(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mo>∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla^{2}J(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math> is a continuous function on the compact set <math id="S4.p4.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists a constant <math id="S4.p4.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S4.p4.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sup_{\theta\in C}\|\nabla^{2}J(\theta)\|\leq L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>sup</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sup_{\theta\in C}\|\nabla^{2}J(\theta)\|\leq L</annotation></semantics></math>. By the mean-value theorem, we then have for any <math id="S4.p4.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{1},\theta_{2}\in C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{1},\theta_{2}\in C</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S4.E10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\nabla J(\theta_{1})-\nabla J(\theta_{2})\|\leq L\|\theta_{1}-\theta_{2}\|." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\nabla J(\theta_{1})-\nabla J(\theta_{2})\|\leq L\|\theta_{1}-\theta_{2}\|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">The proof for Lipschitz continuity of <math id="S4.p4.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla^{2}J(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mo>∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla^{2}J(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math> follows similarly.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 1. ‣ 4 Assumptions ‣ Finite-time analysis of Multi-timescale Stochastic Optimization Algorithms" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> ensures that
the gradient and Hessian vary smoothly along the parameter trajectory and are
used to control drift terms in the finite-time analysis.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 2</span></span><span id="Thmlemma2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under Assumptions <a href="#Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 1. ‣ 4 Assumptions ‣ Finite-time analysis of Multi-timescale Stochastic Optimization Algorithms" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>-<a href="#Thmassumption2" title="Assumption 2. ‣ 4 Assumptions ‣ Finite-time analysis of Multi-timescale Stochastic Optimization Algorithms" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\displaystyle\sup_{\theta\in C}\mathbb{E}[h(\theta,X)^{4}]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle\sup_{\theta\in C}\mathbb{E}[h(\theta,X)^{4}]}</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S4.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Note that</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[h(\theta,X)^{4}]=\sum_{i=1}^{N}d_{\theta}(i)h(\theta,i)^{4}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[h(\theta,X)^{4}]=\sum_{i=1}^{N}d_{\theta}(i)h(\theta,i)^{4}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">The claim follows since <math id="S4.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h(\theta,i)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h(\theta,i)</annotation></semantics></math> is continuous on <math id="S4.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> by Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption2" title="Assumption 2. ‣ 4 Assumptions ‣ Finite-time analysis of Multi-timescale Stochastic Optimization Algorithms" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> and <math id="S4.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> is compact.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmremark1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmremark1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark 1</span></span><span id="Thmremark1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmremark1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmremark1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmremark1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">It follows from Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma2" title="Lemma 2. ‣ 4 Assumptions ‣ Finite-time analysis of Multi-timescale Stochastic Optimization Algorithms" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> that
the gradient and Hessian estimators have uniformly bounded second moments:</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sup_{m}\mathbb{E}\|\widehat{g}(m)\|^{2}&lt;\infty,\qquad\sup_{m}\mathbb{E}\|H(m)\|_{F}^{2}&lt;\infty." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mi>m</mi></munder><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo rspace="1.889em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mi>m</mi></munder><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sup_{m}\mathbb{E}\|\widehat{g}(m)\|^{2}&lt;\infty,\qquad\sup_{m}\mathbb{E}\|H(m)\|_{F}^{2}&lt;\infty.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmremark1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmremark1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">These moment bounds are used to bound variance and cross terms arising from stochastic perturbations. Thus, boundedness of moments holds along the algorithm trajectory due to projection.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmassumption3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_assumption">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmassumption3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Assumption 3</span></span><span id="Thmassumption3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmassumption3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmassumption3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmassumption3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The step-sizes <math id="Thmassumption3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a(m),b(m),c(m),m\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a(m),b(m),c(m),m\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> are selected as
<math id="Thmassumption3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a(m)=(1+m)^{-\sigma},\quad c(m)=(1+m)^{-\alpha},\quad b(m)=(1+m)^{-\nu}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a(m)=(1+m)^{-\sigma},\quad c(m)=(1+m)^{-\alpha},\quad b(m)=(1+m)^{-\nu},</annotation></semantics></math>
with exponents satisfying
<math id="Thmassumption3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\nu&lt;\alpha&lt;\sigma&lt;1." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>ν</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\nu&lt;\alpha&lt;\sigma&lt;1.</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p7.1" class="ltx_p">As a consequence of the above, note that <math id="S4.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a(m)=o(c(m))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a(m)=o(c(m))</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c(m)=o(b(m))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c(m)=o(b(m))</annotation></semantics></math>, thus also <math id="S4.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a(m)=o(b(m))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a(m)=o(b(m))</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p8.1" class="ltx_p">We let the operator <math id="S4.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\text{PD}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>PD</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\text{PD}}</annotation></semantics></math> acting on any matrix <math id="S4.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> be specified via <math id="S4.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\text{PD}}(H)=(H+\lambda I)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>PD</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\text{PD}}(H)=(H+\lambda I)</annotation></semantics></math>, for some <math id="S4.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> s.t. <math id="S4.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(H+\lambda I)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(H+\lambda I)</annotation></semantics></math> becomes positive definite.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmassumption4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_assumption">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmassumption4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Assumption 4</span></span><span id="Thmassumption4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmassumption4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmassumption4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmassumption4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">There exists <math id="Thmassumption4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> such that the regularized Hessian approximation
<math id="Thmassumption4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M(m)=(H(m)+\lambda I)^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M(m)=(H(m)+\lambda I)^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>
is uniformly positive definite for all <math id="Thmassumption4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p9.1" class="ltx_p">Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption4" title="Assumption 4. ‣ 4 Assumptions ‣ Finite-time analysis of Multi-timescale Stochastic Optimization Algorithms" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> ensures stability of the Newton-type updates and is
standard in second order stochastic approximation.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">5 </span>Finite-time analysis of NSF1 and GSF1</h2>

<div id="S5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We outline the main ingredients used to prove Theorems <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1 (Finite-Time Hessian Estimation Error). ‣ Step 4: Aggregation and Total Hessian Error ‣ Mean-Squared Error Decomposition of the Hessian Estimate ‣ 5 Finite-time analysis of NSF1 and GSF1 ‣ Finite-time analysis of Multi-timescale Stochastic Optimization Algorithms" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> and <a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2 (Finite-Time Convergence to FOSP). ‣ Final bound ‣ Bound on the Expected Norm of the Gradient ‣ 5 Finite-time analysis of NSF1 and GSF1 ‣ Finite-time analysis of Multi-timescale Stochastic Optimization Algorithms" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>. The full proofs of these results are deferred to the appendix.
We first provide a bound on the mean-squared error associated with the Hessian estimate: <math id="S5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{t+\tau-1}\sum\limits_{m=\tau}^{t}E[\|H(m)-H^{*}(m)\|^{2}_{2}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{t+\tau-1}\sum\limits_{m=\tau}^{t}E[\|H(m)-H^{*}(m)\|^{2}_{2}]</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{*}(m)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{*}(m)</annotation></semantics></math> is the Hessian of the objective function at <math id="S5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta(m)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta(m)</annotation></semantics></math> and then use the result obtained to calculate a bound on the term <math id="S5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min\limits_{0\leq m\leq T}E[\|\nabla J(\theta(m))\|^{2}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min\limits_{0\leq m\leq T}E[\|\nabla J(\theta(m))\|^{2}]</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<section id="S5.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.1 </span>Finite-time analysis of NSF1</h3>

</section>
<section id="S5.SSx1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection">Mean-Squared Error Decomposition of the Hessian Estimate</h3>

<div id="S5.SSx1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SSx1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S5.SSx1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(m)\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(m)\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the Hessian estimate at iteration <math id="S5.SSx1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>,
and let <math id="S5.SSx1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{*}(m)=\nabla^{2}J(\theta(m))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{*}(m)=\nabla^{2}J(\theta(m))</annotation></semantics></math> denote the true (or smoothed) Hessian evaluated at the current parameter iterate <math id="S5.SSx1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta(m)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta(m)</annotation></semantics></math>.
The mean-squared error (MSE) of the Hessian estimate is obtained as</p>
<table id="S5.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\big[\|H(m)-H^{*}(m)\|_{F}^{2}\big]=\sum_{i=1}^{d}\sum_{j=1}^{d}\mathbb{E}\big[(H_{i,j}(m)-H^{*}_{i,j}(m))^{2}\big]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\big[\|H(m)-H^{*}(m)\|_{F}^{2}\big]=\sum_{i=1}^{d}\sum_{j=1}^{d}\mathbb{E}\big[(H_{i,j}(m)-H^{*}_{i,j}(m))^{2}\big].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<section id="S5.SSx1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Step 1: Splitting into diagonal and off-diagonal components</h4>

<div id="S5.SSx1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SSx1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We decompose the total error into diagonal and off-diagonal error components:</p>
<table id="S5.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\big[\|H(m)-H^{*}(m)\|_{F}^{2}\big]=\underbrace{\sum_{i=1}^{d}\mathbb{E}\big[(H_{i,i}(m)-H^{*}_{i,i}(m))^{2}\big]}_{\text{diagonal error}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>diagonal error</mtext></munder></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\big[\|H(m)-H^{*}(m)\|_{F}^{2}\big]=\underbrace{\sum_{i=1}^{d}\mathbb{E}\big[(H_{i,i}(m)-H^{*}_{i,i}(m))^{2}\big]}_{\text{diagonal error}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="S5.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+\\
\underbrace{\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}i,j=1\\
i\neq j\end{subarray}}^{d}\mathbb{E}\big[(H_{i,j}(m)-H^{*}_{i,j}(m))^{2}\big]}_{\text{off-diagonal error}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mi>d</mi></munderover><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>off-diagonal error</mtext></munder></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+\\
\underbrace{\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}i,j=1\\
i\neq j\end{subarray}}^{d}\mathbb{E}\big[(H_{i,j}(m)-H^{*}_{i,j}(m))^{2}\big]}_{\text{off-diagonal error}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S5.SSx1.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SSx1.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We derive the finite-time bound explicitly for the diagonal elements, as analogous arguments apply to the off-diagonal terms.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SSx1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Step 2: Recursion for the diagonal element error</h4>

<div id="S5.SSx1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SSx1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Define the diagonal error term
<math id="S5.SSx1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{i,i}(m):=H_{i,i}(m)-H^{*}_{i,i}(m)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{i,i}(m):=H_{i,i}(m)-H^{*}_{i,i}(m),</annotation></semantics></math>
and consider its stochastic recursion.
Ignoring the projection operator for now, the diagonal element terms in the Hessian update in the NSF1 scheme get updated as</p>
<table id="S5.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{i,i}(m+1)=(1-b(m))H_{i,i}(m)+b(m)\!\frac{\eta_{i}(m)^{2}-1}{\beta^{2}}\,h(X_{m})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mpadded style="width:0.219em;" width="0.219em"><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mpadded></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{i,i}(m+1)=(1-b(m))H_{i,i}(m)+b(m)\!\frac{\eta_{i}(m)^{2}-1}{\beta^{2}}\,h(X_{m}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SSx1.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S5.SSx1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\eta_{i}(m)\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\eta_{i}(m)\}</annotation></semantics></math> are i.i.d. <math id="S5.SSx1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>-distributed perturbations, <math id="S5.SSx1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> is the perturbation scale,
and <math id="S5.SSx1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b(m)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b(m)</annotation></semantics></math> is the Hessian step-size.
Subtracting the true Hessian term <math id="S5.SSx1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{*}_{i,i}(m+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{*}_{i,i}(m+1)</annotation></semantics></math> and rearranging yields the error recursion:</p>
<table id="S5.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.Ex16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\varepsilon_{i,i}(m+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\varepsilon_{i,i}(m+1)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\varepsilon_{i,i}(m)-b(m)\,\varepsilon_{i,i}(m)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\varepsilon_{i,i}(m)-b(m)\,\varepsilon_{i,i}(m)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.Ex17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+b(m)\left(\frac{\eta_{i}(m)^{2}-1}{\beta^{2}}\,h(X_{m})-H^{*}_{i,i}(m)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+b(m)\left(\frac{\eta_{i}(m)^{2}-1}{\beta^{2}}\,h(X_{m})-H^{*}_{i,i}(m)\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.Ex18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\big(H^{*}_{i,i}(m)-H^{*}_{i,i}(m+1)\big)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\big(H^{*}_{i,i}(m)-H^{*}_{i,i}(m+1)\big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S5.SSx1.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SSx1.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Squaring both sides and taking expectations produces the one-step MSE recursion for the diagonal element:

<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break"><math id="S5.SSx1.SSS0.Px2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\big[\varepsilon_{i,i}(m+1)^{2}\big]=\mathbb{E}\big[\varepsilon_{i,i}(m)^{2}\big]-2b(m)\,\mathbb{E}[\varepsilon_{i,i}(m)^{2}]+\\
\text{additional cross terms}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mtext>additional cross terms</mtext></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\big[\varepsilon_{i,i}(m+1)^{2}\big]=\mathbb{E}\big[\varepsilon_{i,i}(m)^{2}\big]-2b(m)\,\mathbb{E}[\varepsilon_{i,i}(m)^{2}]+\\
\text{additional cross terms}.</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SSx1.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Step 3: Expansion into five components</h4>

<div id="S5.SSx1.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SSx1.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The additional terms in the expansion above can be systematically grouped into five categories, corresponding to constants <math id="S5.SSx1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>–<math id="S5.SSx1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{5}</annotation></semantics></math> used in the finite-time bound.
Each term captures a specific stochastic or deterministic contribution to the growth or decay of the mean-squared error:</p>
<table id="S5.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.Ex19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\sum\limits_{m=\tau}^{t}E([\epsilon_{i,i}(m)]^{2})\leq\sum\limits_{m=\tau}^{t}E[\frac{1}{2b(m)}([\epsilon_{i,i}(m)]^{2}-" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover></mstyle><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover></mstyle><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum\limits_{m=\tau}^{t}E([\epsilon_{i,i}(m)]^{2})\leq\sum\limits_{m=\tau}^{t}E[\frac{1}{2b(m)}([\epsilon_{i,i}(m)]^{2}-</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.Ex20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle[\epsilon_{i,i}(m+1)]^{2})]+\sum\limits_{m=\tau}^{t}E[\epsilon_{i,i}(m)[\frac{\eta_{i}^{2}(m)-1}{\beta^{2}}h(x(m))-" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover></mstyle><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle[\epsilon_{i,i}(m+1)]^{2})]+\sum\limits_{m=\tau}^{t}E[\epsilon_{i,i}(m)[\frac{\eta_{i}^{2}(m)-1}{\beta^{2}}h(x(m))-</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.Ex21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle H_{i,i}^{*}(m)]]+\sum\limits_{m=\tau}^{t}E[\frac{1}{b(m)}\epsilon_{i,i}(m)(H_{i,i}^{*}(m)-H_{i,i}^{*}(m+1))]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover></mstyle><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle H_{i,i}^{*}(m)]]+\sum\limits_{m=\tau}^{t}E[\frac{1}{b(m)}\epsilon_{i,i}(m)(H_{i,i}^{*}(m)-H_{i,i}^{*}(m+1))]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.Ex22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle+\sum\limits_{m=\tau}^{t}E[2b(m)[\frac{\eta_{i}^{2}(m)-1}{\beta^{2}}h(x(m))-H_{i,i}(m)]^{2}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover></mstyle><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>b</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\sum\limits_{m=\tau}^{t}E[2b(m)[\frac{\eta_{i}^{2}(m)-1}{\beta^{2}}h(x(m))-H_{i,i}(m)]^{2}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.Ex23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle+\sum\limits_{m=\tau}^{t}E[\frac{1}{b(m)}(H_{i,i}^{*}(m)-H_{i,i}^{*}(m+1))^{2}]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover></mstyle><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\sum\limits_{m=\tau}^{t}E[\frac{1}{b(m)}(H_{i,i}^{*}(m)-H_{i,i}^{*}(m+1))^{2}].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S5.SSx1.SSS0.Px3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SSx1.SSS0.Px3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The five constants correspond to the following sources:</p>
<ul id="S5.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S5.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S5.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S5.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{1}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">:</span> Uniform bound on the squared estimation error
<math id="S5.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(H_{i,i}(m)-H^{*}_{i,i}(m))^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(H_{i,i}(m)-H^{*}_{i,i}(m))^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>,
obtained from the projection of <math id="S5.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(m)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(m)</annotation></semantics></math> and boundedness of <math id="S5.I1.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{*}(m)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{*}(m)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S5.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S5.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S5.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{2}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">:</span> Cross-term involving <math id="S5.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\eta_{i}^{2}-1)h(X_{m})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\eta_{i}^{2}-1)h(X_{m})</annotation></semantics></math>,
arising from the stochastic perturbation noise.
Bounded by Cauchy–Schwarz using finite moments of <math id="S5.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.I1.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h(X_{m})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h(X_{m})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S5.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S5.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S5.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{3}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">:</span> Coupling term capturing the variation of the true Hessian
<math id="S5.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{*}(m+1)-H^{*}(m)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{*}(m+1)-H^{*}(m)</annotation></semantics></math>;
controlled by the Lipschitz continuity of the Hessian and the step-size relation <math id="S5.I1.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a(m)/b(m)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a(m)/b(m)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S5.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S5.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S5.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{4}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">:</span> Martingale variance term
due to the zero-mean stochastic component in the update, whose contribution can be bounded due to zero-mean perturbations and the boundedness of the Hessian estimates.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S5.I1.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S5.I1.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I1.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S5.I1.i5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{5}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I1.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">:</span> Squared deterministic drift term associated with
<math id="S5.I1.i5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|H^{*}(m+1)-H^{*}(m)\|_{F}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|H^{*}(m+1)-H^{*}(m)\|_{F}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>;
bounded using the Lipschitz property of <math id="S5.I1.i5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>H</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> and the controlled parameter increments.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SSx1.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Step 4: Aggregation and Total Hessian Error</h4>

<div id="S5.SSx1.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SSx1.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Summing the bounds across all diagonal elements
and applying analogous (simpler) arguments to the off-diagonal terms yields</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 1</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(<span id="Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Finite-Time Hessian Estimation Error).</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under Assumptions <a href="#Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 1. ‣ 4 Assumptions ‣ Finite-time analysis of Multi-timescale Stochastic Optimization Algorithms" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>–<a href="#Thmassumption4" title="Assumption 4. ‣ 4 Assumptions ‣ Finite-time analysis of Multi-timescale Stochastic Optimization Algorithms" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>, consider the Hessian estimate <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(m)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(m)</annotation></semantics></math> generated by the NSF1 algorithm and let <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{*}(m)=\nabla^{2}J(\theta(m))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{*}(m)=\nabla^{2}J(\theta(m))</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, for all <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, the mean-squared error satisfies</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\big[\|H(t)-H^{*}(t)\|_{F}^{2}\big]\leq\mathcal{O}\big(t^{\nu}\big)\;+\;\mathcal{O}\big(t^{1-\nu}\big)\;+\;\mathcal{O}\big(t^{\,1-2(\sigma-\nu)}\big)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mi>ν</mi></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mn> 1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\big[\|H(t)-H^{*}(t)\|_{F}^{2}\big]\leq\mathcal{O}\big(t^{\nu}\big)\;+\;\mathcal{O}\big(t^{1-\nu}\big)\;+\;\mathcal{O}\big(t^{\,1-2(\sigma-\nu)}\big),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where the step-size exponents satisfy <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\nu&lt;\alpha&lt;\sigma&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>ν</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\nu&lt;\alpha&lt;\sigma&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">In particular, the Hessian estimation error is governed by the interaction between the Hessian update rate and the drift induced by the parameter updates.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S5.SSx2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection">Bound on the Expected Norm of the Gradient</h3>

<div id="S5.SSx2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SSx2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This section establishes a finite-time upper bound on the expected squared norm of the gradient, thereby quantifying the convergence rate of the proposed algorithm. The derivation follows from the smoothness of <math id="S5.SSx2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math>, the parameter update dynamics, and the finite-time error bounds on the Hessian and gradient estimates.</p>
</div>
<section id="S5.SSx2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Parameter update and smoothness inequality</h4>

<div id="S5.SSx2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SSx2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Recall that the parameter update (without the projection) is</p>
<table id="S5.Ex25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta(m+1)=\theta(m)-a(m)\,M(m)\,Z(m)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta(m+1)=\theta(m)-a(m)\,M(m)\,Z(m),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SSx2.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Using the <math id="S5.SSx2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>-smoothness of <math id="S5.SSx2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math> (from Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 1. ‣ 4 Assumptions ‣ Finite-time analysis of Multi-timescale Stochastic Optimization Algorithms" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>), we have</p>
<table id="S5.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.Ex26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle J(\theta(m+1))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle J(\theta(m+1))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex26.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq J(\theta(m))+\langle\nabla J(\theta(m)),\theta(m+1)-\theta(m)\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq J(\theta(m))+\langle\nabla J(\theta(m)),\theta(m+1)-\theta(m)\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.Ex27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\frac{L}{2}\|\theta(m+1)-\theta(m)\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\frac{L}{2}\|\theta(m+1)-\theta(m)\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.Ex28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=J(\theta(m))-a(m)\langle\nabla J(\theta(m)),M(m)Z(m)\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=J(\theta(m))-a(m)\langle\nabla J(\theta(m)),M(m)Z(m)\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.Ex29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\frac{L}{2}a(m)^{2}\|M(m)z(m)\|^{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\frac{L}{2}a(m)^{2}\|M(m)z(m)\|^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SSx2.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Error decomposition</h4>

<div id="S5.SSx2.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SSx2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Note that</p>
<table id="S5.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.Ex30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle M(m)z(m)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle M(m)z(m)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex30.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=[M(m)-M^{*}(m)]Z(m)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=[M(m)-M^{*}(m)]Z(m)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.Ex31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+M^{*}(m)[Z(m)-Z^{*}(m)]+M^{*}(m)Z^{*}(m)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Z</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>Z</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+M^{*}(m)[Z(m)-Z^{*}(m)]+M^{*}(m)Z^{*}(m),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SSx2.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S5.SSx2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M^{*}(m)=(\nabla^{2}J(\theta(m))+\lambda I)^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M^{*}(m)=(\nabla^{2}J(\theta(m))+\lambda I)^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S5.SSx2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z^{*}(m)=\nabla J(\theta(m))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Z</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z^{*}(m)=\nabla J(\theta(m))</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively. Substituting and rearranging gives</p>
<table id="S5.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.Ex32"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle J(\theta(m+1))\leq J(\theta(m))-a(m)\langle\nabla J(\theta(m)),[M(m)-M^{*}(m)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">J</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">θ</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">m</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">≤</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">J</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">θ</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">m</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">a</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">m</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">J</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">θ</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">m</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">[</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">M</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">m</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">M</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">∗</mo></msup><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">m</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle J(\theta(m+1))\leq J(\theta(m))-a(m)\langle\nabla J(\theta(m)),[M(m)-M^{*}(m)]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.Ex33"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle Z(m)\rangle-a(m)\langle\nabla J(\theta(m)),M^{*}(m)[Z(m)-Z^{*}(m)]\rangle-" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">Z</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">m</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">a</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">m</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">J</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">θ</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">m</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">M</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">∗</mo></msup><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">m</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">[</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">Z</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">m</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">Z</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">∗</mo></msup><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">m</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Z(m)\rangle-a(m)\langle\nabla J(\theta(m)),M^{*}(m)[Z(m)-Z^{*}(m)]\rangle-</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.Ex34"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle a(m)\langle\nabla J(\theta(m)),M^{*}(m)\nabla J(\theta(m))\rangle+\frac{L}{2}a(m)^{2}\|M(m)Z(m)\|^{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">a</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">m</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">J</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">θ</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">m</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">M</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">∗</mo></msup><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">m</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" rspace="0.167em">)</mo></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">J</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">θ</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">m</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi mathsize="0.900em">L</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mi mathsize="0.900em">a</mi><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">m</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">M</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">m</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">Z</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">m</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><msup><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.0835em" mathsize="0.900em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle a(m)\langle\nabla J(\theta(m)),M^{*}(m)\nabla J(\theta(m))\rangle+\frac{L}{2}a(m)^{2}\|M(m)Z(m)\|^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SSx2.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Bounding the gradient term</h4>

<div id="S5.SSx2.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SSx2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="S5.SSx2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M^{*}(m)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M^{*}(m)</annotation></semantics></math> is positive definite with the smallest eigenvalue <math id="S5.SSx2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{c}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{c}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="S5.SSx2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{\top}M^{*}(m)x\geq\lambda_{c}\|x\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{\top}M^{*}(m)x\geq\lambda_{c}\|x\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="S5.SSx2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>.
Therefore,</p>
<table id="S5.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.Ex35"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle a(m)\lambda_{c}\|\nabla J(\theta(m))\|^{2}\leq(J(\theta(m))-J(\theta(m+1)))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle a(m)\lambda_{c}\|\nabla J(\theta(m))\|^{2}\leq(J(\theta(m))-J(\theta(m+1)))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.Ex36"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-a(m)\langle\nabla J(\theta(m)),[M(m)-M^{*}(m)]Z(m)\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-a(m)\langle\nabla J(\theta(m)),[M(m)-M^{*}(m)]Z(m)\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.Ex37"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-a(m)\langle\nabla J(\theta(m)),M^{*}(m)[Z(m)-Z^{*}(m)]\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Z</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-a(m)\langle\nabla J(\theta(m)),M^{*}(m)[Z(m)-Z^{*}(m)]\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.Ex38"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\frac{L}{2}a(m)^{2}\|M(m)Z(m)\|^{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\frac{L}{2}a(m)^{2}\|M(m)Z(m)\|^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S5.SSx2.SSS0.Px3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SSx2.SSS0.Px3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Dividing by <math id="S5.SSx2.SSS0.Px3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a(m)\lambda_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a(m)\lambda_{c}</annotation></semantics></math> and taking expectations yields</p>
<table id="S5.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.Ex39"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\|\nabla J(\theta(m))\|^{2}\leq\frac{1}{a(m)\lambda_{c}}\mathbb{E}[J(\theta(m))-J(\theta(m+1))]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\|\nabla J(\theta(m))\|^{2}\leq\frac{1}{a(m)\lambda_{c}}\mathbb{E}[J(\theta(m))-J(\theta(m+1))]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.Ex40"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-\frac{1}{\lambda_{c}}\mathbb{E}\langle\nabla J(\theta(m)),[M(m)-M^{*}(m)]Z(m)\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\frac{1}{\lambda_{c}}\mathbb{E}\langle\nabla J(\theta(m)),[M(m)-M^{*}(m)]Z(m)\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.Ex41"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-\frac{1}{\lambda_{c}}\mathbb{E}\langle\nabla J(\theta(m)),M^{*}(m)[Z(m)-Z^{*}(m)]\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Z</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\frac{1}{\lambda_{c}}\mathbb{E}\langle\nabla J(\theta(m)),M^{*}(m)[Z(m)-Z^{*}(m)]\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.Ex42"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\frac{La(m)}{2\lambda_{c}}\mathbb{E}\|M(m)Z(m)\|^{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\frac{La(m)}{2\lambda_{c}}\mathbb{E}\|M(m)Z(m)\|^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SSx2.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Summation and term-wise bounding</h4>

<div id="S5.SSx2.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SSx2.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Summing over <math id="S5.SSx2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=\tau</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S5.SSx2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> produces</p>
<table id="S5.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.Ex43"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex43.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{m=\tau}^{t}\mathbb{E}\|\nabla J(\theta(m))\|^{2}\leq\sum_{m=\tau}^{t}\Bigg[\frac{\mathbb{E}[J(\theta(m))-J(\theta(m+1))]}{a(m)\lambda_{c}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" movablelimits="false" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">m</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">τ</mi></mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></munderover></mstyle><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">J</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">θ</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">m</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><msup><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.0835em" mathsize="0.900em">≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" movablelimits="false" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">m</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">τ</mi></mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">m</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">m</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">m</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">λ</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">c</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{m=\tau}^{t}\mathbb{E}\|\nabla J(\theta(m))\|^{2}\leq\sum_{m=\tau}^{t}\Bigg[\frac{\mathbb{E}[J(\theta(m))-J(\theta(m+1))]}{a(m)\lambda_{c}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.Ex44"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\frac{1}{\lambda_{c}}\mathbb{E}\langle\nabla J(\theta(m)),-[M(m)-M^{*}(m)]Z(m)\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">λ</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">c</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">J</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">m</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">m</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">M</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">m</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">Z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">m</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\frac{1}{\lambda_{c}}\mathbb{E}\langle\nabla J(\theta(m)),-[M(m)-M^{*}(m)]Z(m)\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.Ex45"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\frac{1}{\lambda_{c}}\mathbb{E}\langle\nabla J(\theta(m)),-M^{*}(m)[Z(m)-Z^{*}(m)]\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">λ</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">c</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">J</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">m</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">M</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">m</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">Z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">m</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">Z</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">m</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\frac{1}{\lambda_{c}}\mathbb{E}\langle\nabla J(\theta(m)),-M^{*}(m)[Z(m)-Z^{*}(m)]\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.Ex46"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex46.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle+\frac{La(m)}{2\lambda_{c}}\mathbb{E}\|M(m)Z(m)\|^{2}\Bigg]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">m</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">λ</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">c</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">M</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">m</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">Z</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">m</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><msup><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn></msup><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">]</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.900em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\frac{La(m)}{2\lambda_{c}}\mathbb{E}\|M(m)Z(m)\|^{2}\Bigg].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SSx2.SSS0.Px4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Each of the four summation terms is bounded individually:</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SSx2.SSS0.Px4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="S5.I2" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S5.I2.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S5.I2.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I2.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.I2.ix1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Objective decrease:</span>
By telescoping and boundedness of <math id="S5.I2.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>J</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="S5.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.Ex47"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{m=\tau}^{t}\frac{\mathbb{E}[J(\theta(m))-J(\theta(m+1))]}{a(m)\lambda_{c}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{m=\tau}^{t}\frac{\mathbb{E}[J(\theta(m))-J(\theta(m+1))]}{a(m)\lambda_{c}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex47.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{C_{1}}{a(t)}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{C_{1}}{a(t)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="S5.I2.ix2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S5.I2.ix2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I2.ix2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.I2.ix2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Matrix approximation error:</span>
Using Cauchy–Schwarz inequality and bounds <math id="S5.I2.ix2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|z(m)\|\leq C_{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>G</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|z(m)\|\leq C_{G}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="S5.EGx10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.Ex48"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{m=\tau}^{t}\!\frac{1}{\lambda_{c}}\mathbb{E}\langle\nabla J(\theta(m)),-[M(m)-M^{*}(m)]Z(m)\rangle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" movablelimits="false" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">m</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">τ</mi></mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">λ</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">c</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">J</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">m</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">m</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">M</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">m</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">Z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">m</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">≤</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{m=\tau}^{t}\!\frac{1}{\lambda_{c}}\mathbb{E}\langle\nabla J(\theta(m)),-[M(m)-M^{*}(m)]Z(m)\rangle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.Ex49"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle C_{2}\sqrt{\sum_{m=\tau}^{t}\mathbb{E}\|\nabla J(\theta(m))\|^{2}}\sqrt{\sum_{m=\tau}^{t}\mathbb{E}\|M(m)-M^{*}(m)\|_{F}^{2}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">C</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" movablelimits="false" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">m</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">τ</mi></mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">J</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">m</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" movablelimits="false" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">m</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">τ</mi></mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">m</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">M</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">m</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">F</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.900em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle C_{2}\sqrt{\sum_{m=\tau}^{t}\mathbb{E}\|\nabla J(\theta(m))\|^{2}}\sqrt{\sum_{m=\tau}^{t}\mathbb{E}\|M(m)-M^{*}(m)\|_{F}^{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="S5.I2.ix3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(3)</span> 
<div id="S5.I2.ix3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I2.ix3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.I2.ix3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Gradient estimation error:</span>
Since <math id="S5.I2.ix3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|M^{*}(m)\|_{F}\leq C_{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>H</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|M^{*}(m)\|_{F}\leq C_{H}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="S5.EGx11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.Ex50"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{m=\tau}^{t}\ \frac{1}{\lambda_{c}}\mathbb{E}\langle\nabla J(\theta(m)),-M^{*}(m)[Z(m)-Z^{*}(m)]\rangle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" movablelimits="false" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">m</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">τ</mi></mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">λ</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">c</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">J</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">m</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">M</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">m</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">Z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">m</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">Z</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">m</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">≤</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{m=\tau}^{t}\ \frac{1}{\lambda_{c}}\mathbb{E}\langle\nabla J(\theta(m)),-M^{*}(m)[Z(m)-Z^{*}(m)]\rangle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.Ex51"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle C_{3}\sqrt{\sum_{m=\tau}^{t}\mathbb{E}\|\nabla J(\theta(m))\|^{2}}\sqrt{\sum_{m=\tau}^{t}\mathbb{E}\|Z(m)-Z^{*}(m)\|^{2}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">C</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" movablelimits="false" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">m</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">τ</mi></mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">J</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">m</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" movablelimits="false" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">m</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">τ</mi></mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">Z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">m</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">Z</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">m</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.900em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle C_{3}\sqrt{\sum_{m=\tau}^{t}\mathbb{E}\|\nabla J(\theta(m))\|^{2}}\sqrt{\sum_{m=\tau}^{t}\mathbb{E}\|Z(m)-Z^{*}(m)\|^{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.I2.ix3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The values of the constants <math id="S5.I2.ix3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{1}-C_{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{1}-C_{4}</annotation></semantics></math> have been stated in proofs in the appendix.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S5.I2.ix4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(4)</span> 
<div id="S5.I2.ix4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I2.ix4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.I2.ix4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Higher-order step-size term:</span></p>
<table id="S5.EGx12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.Ex52"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{m=\tau}^{t}\!\frac{La(m)}{2\lambda_{c}}\mathbb{E}\|M(m)z(m)\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{m=\tau}^{t}\!\frac{La(m)}{2\lambda_{c}}\mathbb{E}\|M(m)z(m)\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex52.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq C_{4}\sum_{m=\tau}^{t}a(m)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq C_{4}\sum_{m=\tau}^{t}a(m).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SSx2.SSS0.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Aggregated bound</h4>

<div id="S5.SSx2.SSS0.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SSx2.SSS0.Px5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Combining all the terms, we obtain</p>
<table id="S5.EGx13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.Ex53"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex53.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{m=\tau}^{t}\mathbb{E}\|\nabla J(\theta(m))\|^{2}\leq\frac{C_{1}}{a(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" movablelimits="false" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">m</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">τ</mi></mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">J</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">m</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">C</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></msub><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{m=\tau}^{t}\mathbb{E}\|\nabla J(\theta(m))\|^{2}\leq\frac{C_{1}}{a(t)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.Ex54"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex54.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+C_{2}\sqrt{\sum_{m=\tau}^{t}\mathbb{E}\|\nabla J(\theta(m))\|^{2}}\sqrt{\sum_{m=\tau}^{t}\mathbb{E}\|M(m)-M^{*}(m)\|_{F}^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">C</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" movablelimits="false" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">m</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">τ</mi></mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">J</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">m</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" movablelimits="false" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">m</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">τ</mi></mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">m</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">M</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">m</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">F</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+C_{2}\sqrt{\sum_{m=\tau}^{t}\mathbb{E}\|\nabla J(\theta(m))\|^{2}}\sqrt{\sum_{m=\tau}^{t}\mathbb{E}\|M(m)-M^{*}(m)\|_{F}^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.Ex55"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex55.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+C_{3}\sqrt{\sum_{m=\tau}^{t}\mathbb{E}\|\nabla J(\theta(m))\|^{2}}\sqrt{\sum_{m=\tau}^{t}\mathbb{E}\|Z(m)-Z^{*}(m)\|^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">C</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" movablelimits="false" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">m</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">τ</mi></mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">J</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">m</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" movablelimits="false" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">m</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">τ</mi></mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">Z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">m</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">Z</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">m</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+C_{3}\sqrt{\sum_{m=\tau}^{t}\mathbb{E}\|\nabla J(\theta(m))\|^{2}}\sqrt{\sum_{m=\tau}^{t}\mathbb{E}\|Z(m)-Z^{*}(m)\|^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.Ex56"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex56.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle+C_{4}\sum_{m=\tau}^{t}a(m)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">C</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">4</mn></msub><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" movablelimits="false" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">m</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">τ</mi></mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></munderover></mstyle><mi mathsize="0.900em">a</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">m</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.900em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+C_{4}\sum_{m=\tau}^{t}a(m).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SSx2.SSS0.Px6" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Substituting step-size schedules</h4>

<div id="S5.SSx2.SSS0.Px6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SSx2.SSS0.Px6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Now substitute <math id="S5.SSx2.SSS0.Px6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a(m)=(1+m)^{-\sigma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a(m)=(1+m)^{-\sigma}</annotation></semantics></math> and use the finite-time bounds
<math id="S5.SSx2.SSS0.Px6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\|M(m)-M^{*}(m)\|^{2}=O(m^{\nu-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>M</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\|M(m)-M^{*}(m)\|^{2}=O(m^{\nu-1})</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="S5.SSx2.SSS0.Px6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\|z(m)-z^{*}(m)\|^{2}=O(m^{\alpha-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\|z(m)-z^{*}(m)\|^{2}=O(m^{\alpha-1})</annotation></semantics></math>
with <math id="S5.SSx2.SSS0.Px6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\nu&lt;\alpha&lt;\sigma&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>ν</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\nu&lt;\alpha&lt;\sigma&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SSx2.SSS0.Px7" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Final bound</h4>

<div id="S5.SSx2.SSS0.Px7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SSx2.SSS0.Px7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="S5.SSx2.SSS0.Px7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min\limits_{0\leq m\leq T}\mathbb{E}\|\nabla J(\theta(m))\|^{2}\leq\frac{1}{1+T}\sum_{m=0}^{T}\mathbb{E}\|\nabla J(\theta(m))\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>𝔼</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min\limits_{0\leq m\leq T}\mathbb{E}\|\nabla J(\theta(m))\|^{2}\leq\frac{1}{1+T}\sum_{m=0}^{T}\mathbb{E}\|\nabla J(\theta(m))\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain the following result on finite-time convergence to first-order stationary points(FOSP).</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 2</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Finite-Time Convergence to FOSP)<span id="Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under Assumptions 1–4, the iterates of the NSF1 algorithm, for any horizon <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, satisfy</span></p>
<table id="S5.EGx14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.Ex57"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex57.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\min_{0\leq m\leq T}\mathbb{E}\|\nabla J(\theta(m))\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>𝔼</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\min_{0\leq m\leq T}\mathbb{E}\|\nabla J(\theta(m))\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex57.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\mathcal{O}\big(T^{\sigma-1}\big)+\mathcal{O}\big(T^{-\nu}\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\mathcal{O}\big(T^{\sigma-1}\big)+\mathcal{O}\big(T^{-\nu}\big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.Ex58"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex58.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\mathcal{O}\big(T^{-2(\sigma-\alpha)}\big)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\mathcal{O}\big(T^{-2(\sigma-\alpha)}\big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The algorithm converges to a FOSP at a sublinear rate determined by the step-size exponents and the propagation of gradient and Hessian estimation errors.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SSx2.SSS0.Px8" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Interpretation</h4>

<div id="S5.SSx2.SSS0.Px8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="S5.I3" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S5.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S5.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The term <math id="S5.I3.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(T^{\sigma-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(T^{\sigma-1})</annotation></semantics></math> represents the dominant convergence rate induced by the parameter step-size <math id="S5.I3.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a(m)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a(m)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S5.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S5.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The terms <math id="S5.I3.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(T^{-\nu})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(T^{-\nu})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.I3.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(T^{-2(\sigma-\alpha)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(T^{-2(\sigma-\alpha)})</annotation></semantics></math> capture the finite-time propagation of estimation errors from the matrix (<math id="S5.I3.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M(m)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M(m)</annotation></semantics></math>) and gradient (<math id="S5.I3.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z(m)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z(m)</annotation></semantics></math>) updates.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S5.I3.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S5.I3.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I3.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="S5.I3.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\nu&lt;\alpha&lt;\sigma&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>ν</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\nu&lt;\alpha&lt;\sigma&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, all terms vanish asymptotically, establishing sublinear convergence in expectation.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="S5.SSx2.SSS0.Px8.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SSx2.SSS0.Px8.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Thus, under Assumptions <a href="#Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 1. ‣ 4 Assumptions ‣ Finite-time analysis of Multi-timescale Stochastic Optimization Algorithms" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>–<a href="#Thmassumption4" title="Assumption 4. ‣ 4 Assumptions ‣ Finite-time analysis of Multi-timescale Stochastic Optimization Algorithms" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> and the three-timescale step-size design, the algorithm achieves a finite-time bound on the expected squared gradient norm that ensures the convergence of the sequence <math id="S5.SSx2.SSS0.Px8.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\theta(m)\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\theta(m)\}</annotation></semantics></math> to a stationary point.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SSx2.SSS0.Px8.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SSx2.SSS0.Px8.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Solving for the optimal rate of convergence, we get <math id="S5.SSx2.SSS0.Px8.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu\rightarrow 0.4,\alpha\rightarrow\nu," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0.4</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu\rightarrow 0.4,\alpha\rightarrow\nu,</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SSx2.SSS0.Px8.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma\rightarrow 0.6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0.6</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma\rightarrow 0.6</annotation></semantics></math> gives the optimal rate of the order <math id="S5.SSx2.SSS0.Px8.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(-0.4+\delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>0.4</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(-0.4+\delta)</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S5.SSx2.SSS0.Px8.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\rightarrow 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\rightarrow 0</annotation></semantics></math>. These values are obtained by balancing the dominant finite-time error terms.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SSx2.SSS0.Px9" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Conclusion</h4>

<div id="S5.SSx2.SSS0.Px9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SSx2.SSS0.Px9.p1.1" class="ltx_p">All constants <math id="S5.SSx2.SSS0.Px9.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>–<math id="S5.SSx2.SSS0.Px9.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{5}</annotation></semantics></math> are thus finite and depend only on the fixed quantities
<math id="S5.SSx2.SSS0.Px9.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(B_{Z},L,L_{H},C_{\theta},H_{h},\beta,d,c)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(B_{Z},L,L_{H},C_{\theta},H_{h},\beta,d,c)</annotation></semantics></math>.
No additional requirements beyond Assumptions <a href="#Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 1. ‣ 4 Assumptions ‣ Finite-time analysis of Multi-timescale Stochastic Optimization Algorithms" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>–<a href="#Thmassumption4" title="Assumption 4. ‣ 4 Assumptions ‣ Finite-time analysis of Multi-timescale Stochastic Optimization Algorithms" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> are needed.
The bounds follow directly from standard norm inequalities,
Lipschitz smoothness of the objective,
and bounded-moment conditions on the stochastic perturbations.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.2 </span>Finite time analysis of GSF1 </h3>

<div id="Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 3</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>( Finite-Time Gradient Estimation Error)<span id="Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under Assumptions <a href="#Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 1. ‣ 4 Assumptions ‣ Finite-time analysis of Multi-timescale Stochastic Optimization Algorithms" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>–<a href="#Thmassumption4" title="Assumption 4. ‣ 4 Assumptions ‣ Finite-time analysis of Multi-timescale Stochastic Optimization Algorithms" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>, consider the Hessian estimate <math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(m)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(m)</annotation></semantics></math> generated by the NSF1 algorithm and let <math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z^{*}(m)=\nabla J(\theta(m))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z^{*}(m)=\nabla J(\theta(m))</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, for all <math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, the mean-squared error satisfies</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex59" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex59.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\big[\|z(t)-z^{*}(t)\|_{F}^{2}\big]\leq\mathcal{O}\big(t^{\alpha}\big)\;+\;\mathcal{O}\big(t^{1-\alpha}\big)\;+\;\mathcal{O}\big(t^{\,1-2(\sigma-\alpha)}\big)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mi>α</mi></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mn> 1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\big[\|z(t)-z^{*}(t)\|_{F}^{2}\big]\leq\mathcal{O}\big(t^{\alpha}\big)\;+\;\mathcal{O}\big(t^{1-\alpha}\big)\;+\;\mathcal{O}\big(t^{\,1-2(\sigma-\alpha)}\big),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where the step-size exponents satisfy <math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\alpha&lt;\sigma&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\alpha&lt;\sigma&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 4</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Finite-Time Convergence to FOSP)<span id="Thmtheorem4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under Assumptions 1–4, the iterates of the GSF1 algorithm, for any horizon <math id="Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, satisfy</span></p>
<table id="S5.EGx15" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.Ex60"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex60.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\min_{0\leq m\leq T}\mathbb{E}\|\nabla J(\theta(m))\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>𝔼</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\min_{0\leq m\leq T}\mathbb{E}\|\nabla J(\theta(m))\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex60.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\mathcal{O}(t^{\sigma-1})+\mathcal{O}(t^{-\alpha})+\mathcal{O}(t^{-2(\sigma-\alpha)}).." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">.</mo><mo lspace="0.0835em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\mathcal{O}(t^{\sigma-1})+\mathcal{O}(t^{-\alpha})+\mathcal{O}(t^{-2(\sigma-\alpha)})..</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Setting <math id="S5.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=0.4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=0.4</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma=0.6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.6</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma=0.6</annotation></semantics></math> in Theorem 4 gives us the optimal rate of convergence, i.e., <math id="S5.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(t^{-0.4})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>0.4</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(t^{-0.4}).</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Proofs of both the theorems have been discussed in the appendix.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S6" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">6 </span>Experiments and Results</h2>

<section id="S6.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">6.1 </span>Experimental Setup</h3>

<div id="S6.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We evaluate the proposed GSF1 and N-SF1 algorithms on a continuous-control benchmark derived from the MountainCar environment in reinforcement learning <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">16</a>]</cite>. For ease of implementation, we consider the Jacobi version of the N-SF1 algorithm where the Hessian is replaced by a diagonal matrix with diagonal entries corresponding to those of the Hessian and off-diagonal entries set to zero <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">6</a>]</cite>. To match the theoretical setting of long-run average cost optimization, we implement a <em id="S6.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">custom infinite-horizon simulator</em> in which the system dynamics evolve indefinitely without terminal states or episodic resets.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The system state is given by the car’s position and velocity, and the control input is a continuous force bounded in <math id="S6.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[-1,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[-1,1]</annotation></semantics></math>. The dynamics follow the standard MountainCar equations with a small additive Gaussian noise. The running cost is defined as</p>
<table id="S6.Ex61" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex61.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h(x,u)=0.1\,u^{2}+(x-x^{\star})^{2}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>0.1</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h(x,u)=0.1\,u^{2}+(x-x^{\star})^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S6.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{\star}=0.45" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0.45</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{\star}=0.45</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the target position. This cost is smooth, bounded, and satisfies the regularity assumptions required for the finite-time analysis.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The policy is parameterized by a two-layer neural network with <math id="S6.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tanh" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>tanh</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tanh</annotation></semantics></math> activations. Both algorithms operate in the <em id="S6.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">average-cost</em> setting, using per-step costs rather than episodic returns. Performance is evaluated by estimating the steady-state average cost over long rollouts, with evaluations performed periodically during training.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">All experiments are conducted using a single long trajectory per run. We have presented the results of our experiments in figure <a href="#S6.F1" title="Figure 1 ‣ 6.3 Summary of Experimental Findings ‣ 6 Experiments and Results ‣ Finite-time analysis of Multi-timescale Stochastic Optimization Algorithms" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, which were obtained by taking average over 5 random seeds.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S6.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">6.2 </span>Hyperparameter Configuration</h3>

<div id="S6.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#S6.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ 6.3 Summary of Experimental Findings ‣ 6 Experiments and Results ‣ Finite-time analysis of Multi-timescale Stochastic Optimization Algorithms" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> summarizes the hyperparameters used for G-SF1 and diagonal N-SF1. Step sizes are chosen to satisfy the required time-scale separation conditions in the finite-time analysis, with the parameter update evolving on the slowest time scale.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S6.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">6.3 </span>Summary of Experimental Findings</h3>

<div id="S6.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The experimental results shown in the figures below confirm the key theoretical insights of this work. Both G-SF1 and N-SF1 converge in the average-cost setting as predicted, with finite-time behavior strongly influenced by estimator variance.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S6.F1" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2603.29380v1/pap_nsf.png" id="S6.F1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:678/509;" width="678" height="509" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S6.F1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 1</span>: </span><span id="S6.F1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Convergence of algorithms for Mountain Car environment</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="S6.T1" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S6.T1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 1</span>: </span><span id="S6.T1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Hyperparameters used for GSF1 and diagonal NSF1 experiments</span></figcaption>
<table id="S6.T1.4" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="S6.T1.4.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S6.T1.4.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt">Hyperparameter</th>
<th id="S6.T1.4.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt">GSF1</th>
